mod:place_too_deep;
// A PLACE 64 OR MORE STORAGE STEPS FROM ITS ROOT IS REFUSED WHERE IT IS TYPED (DEF-430's class, landing 177d2b4, row 2). The walks that ask a place's root
// (`fixed`, limited, lent, a view, frozen, the `for` party, a lending `pick`'s root, a stateful kind's road) stop at 64 steps (`BORROW_FUEL`), and some
// answered "nothing to refuse" there. The typer now counts a place's storage steps (each `.f`, `[i]`, `[lo...hi]` and `<-`) and refuses a place at 64 or
// more with TYPE-024, as `@` of the same place has been; the `where` guard's move walk starts at the tree's own bound and its end refuses (TYPE-089).
// Each module is one cell; a cell's `main` stands here as `cell_main_<cell>`. Faces, each a fault on 6d059fd:
//   `fxl_64`, `fxs_64` (H3): a range of a `fixed` array 64 deep is a writable view of read-only memory (79; 97 at -O0, 59 at -O2).
//   `fp_64`, `fd_64`, `fi_64` (H4): a `for` over a place whose 64th step is a field, a dereference or an index frees what it reads (83; 97 under the detector).
//   `fk_64`, `fkc_0_64` (H5): a lending `pick` 64 steps deep isn't frozen (83; 97).
//   `gm_31`, `gms_31` (H1): the move of the arm's own binding 31 calls down a `where` guard was not seen (83; 97); TYPE-089 now.
//   `sk_cv_f_64`, `sk_cv_z_64`, `sk_cv_l_64`, `sk_gd_v_64`: a stateful kind's operation 64 steps down a `fixed`, a frozen, a lent and a viewed place ran
//   (69, 67): every kind measured so (Mutex, Guard, RwLock, RGuard, CondVar, Barrier, Channel, SharedArena), two stand here.
// H2 (the loop's havoc missing a write 31 calls down, `--elide` removing a live guard) is a verified-build face, not a refusal: no cell here.
// 2026-11-08, landing 177d2b4 (row 2; management_30's ruling of 02:03): three cells from DEF-595's files, whose own cells are re-spelled under 64 there.
//   `zd2k_source_chain_d70` (list_ptr_for_binding.npk, lines 1214-1323 of 6d059fd's text) and `zd7t_pile_60_loops2_chain100` (lines 2121-2561): 236 on
//   main (97 under the detector), BORROW-015 on 6d059fd, TYPE-024 now. Their faces at these depths are closed by Part A, no longer measured by DEF-595's walk.
//   `zd4c_loops2_chain100_ctl` (list_ptr_for_binding_ok.npk, lines 244-684): a right program (67 on main and 6d059fd), a NAMED PRICE: a `for` over an
//   iterable 100 storage steps deep, refused as `@` of such a place is.
// 63 steps keep their own roads; the right programs at 63 steps, the split at a pointer and the deepest right guard and loop are `place_too_deep_ok.npk`.
error:E5;
